  "question": {
    "text": "A function is matched below against an interval where it is supposed to be increasing. Which of the following pairs is incorrectly matched?\n$Interval \\rightarrow Function$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gIklw",
      "text": "\n$(-\\infty, \\infty) \\rightarrow x^3-3 x^2+3 x+3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XoJeQ",
      "text": "\n$[2, \\infty) \\rightarrow 2x^3-3 x^2-12 x+6$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aDknU",
      "text": "\n$\\left(-\\infty, \\frac{1}{3}\\right] \\rightarrow \\quad 3 x^2-2 x+1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "fPjjV",
      "text": "\n$(-\\infty, -4] \\rightarrow x^3+6 x^2+6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Clearly function $f(x)=3 x^2-2 x+1$ is increasing when $f^{\\prime}(x)=6 x-2 \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow x \\in[1 / 3, \\infty)$\nHence $(C)$ is incorrect.",
    "image": null
  },
